{"availability":"available","full":"flas-ai/FLAS","name":"FLAS","description":"[NeurIPS 2026 Poster] Flow-based Activation Steering for Inference-Time Intervention.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":20,"forks":3,"created":"2026-05-07T08:26:31Z","updated":"2026-09-30T18:55:36Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://flas-ai.github.io","topics":[],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Lunamos/flas-demo","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:03:47.801Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T20:03:47.801Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T20:03:47.801Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:03:47.801Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"x","name":"As Seen On X.com","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2105857929626652823","postId":"2105857929626652823","postedAt":"2026-10-02T03:10:30.000Z"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T20:03:48.128Z","stars":20,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Flow-based Activation Steering for Inference-Time Intervention. NeurIPS 2026 (Poster).","FLAS is a natural-language activation-steering method for LLMs. Where prior work like Golden Gate Claude had to lock in a single behavior in advance, FLAS learns a single general concept-conditioned velocity field $v\\theta(h, t, c)$. At inference you hand it any natural-language concept $c$ and it produces the right inference-time intervention. The same checkpoint handles thousands of unseen concepts, and is the first learned steering method to consistently outperform in-context prompting on AxBench.","This repository provides a unified, multi-family implementation of FLAS. Beyond the Gemma-2 models from the paper, the same flow-based steerer trains on Qwen3, Llama-3.1, and Gemma-3 (base or instruct) through a model-type registry — adding a new family is a single registry entry. The FlowBlock also supports an optional self-attention ablation, and training scales to larger concept corpora (FLAS-46k). The checkpoints and results below are the paper's Gemma-2 artifacts; the other families are trained from scratch with the same recipe."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flas-ai/FLAS/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1263b59f2b9d9e04ea7e61d3ffa35d9df6384826a3dca3fe1ec95ae9f79b7abd","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T20:03:47.801Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T20:03:47.801Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Flow-based Activation Steering for Inference-Time Intervention. NeurIPS 2026 (Poster).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flas-ai/FLAS/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The base LLM (Gemma-2-2B-IT or Gemma-2-9B-IT) is downloaded from Hugging Face on first use; make sure you have run hf auth login and accepted the Gemma-2 license.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flas-ai/FLAS/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Make sure you have run hf login and accepted the relevant model license (e.g.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flas-ai/FLAS/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"1263b59f2b9d9e04ea7e61d3ffa35d9df6384826a3dca3fe1ec95ae9f79b7abd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flas-ai/FLAS/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T20:03:47.801Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-30T18:55:36Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flas-ai/FLAS/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T20:03:47.801Z","hash":"1263b59f2b9d9e04ea7e61d3ffa35d9df6384826a3dca3fe1ec95ae9f79b7abd","originalBytes":13641,"storedBytes":13641,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["axbench","flas","base","run","bash","python","data","layer","single","training","checkpoints","steering","alpaca","concept","concept16k","concept500","eval","results","c500","gemma-2-2b-it","generate","generation","held-out","models","paper","scripts","bf16","evaluation","flas-46k","gemma-2","google","gpt-4o-mini","hub","judge","license","registry","thirdparty","activation","below","da